  "id": "sleep-apnea",
  "term": "sleep apnea",
  "definition": "Sleep apnea, specifically obstructive sleep apnea, is a sleep-related condition in which the upper airway repeatedly narrows or collapses during sleep, causing partial or complete blockage of airflow. If it is not treated, it can contribute to important health problems, including neurocognitive difficulties.",
